# {{ worker_title }} ({{ worker_id }})

A Clonway fleet worker, scaffolded from
[clonway-cockpit](https://github.com/hearth-care/clonway-cockpit)'s worker
template (S8/C6). It is **born with**:

- an interactive **cockpit** — `{{ worker_id }}` (bare, on a TTY) opens the
  three-region shell (pulse / needs-you / toolkit) with one example capability,
  a pulse stub, and a Doctor stub;
- a flag-guarded **Signal emit** path (`{{ worker_id }} signals scan`, gated on
  `{{ emit_flag }}`, default OFF) that writes the C0 wire shape to
  `signals/{{ worker_id }}/latest.jsonl`;
- a **mandatory** `@scan_horizon` stub (`scan_{{ package_name }}_horizon`) — a
  worker can't exist without at least an empty forward scan (proactive by
  construction), guarded by an `xfail` test until you fill it in;
- run/stage **telemetry** (`{{ package_name }}.obs`) to the xops dashboard;
- the single **write-gate + draft-never-send** safety posture, inherited from
  the framework;
- a no-op **home extension seam** (`src/{{ package_name }}/cli/home_hooks.py`) for
  worker-owned panels/rows/keys without forking the shared cockpit shell;
- a commented **Google auth seam** (`src/{{ package_name }}/google_auth.py`) that
  uses `CredentialSpec` instead of copying a token store;
- **CI** (ruff + mypy + pytest).

## Quick start

```bash
uv sync
uv run {{ worker_id }} signals scan                  # -> disabled (flag off)
{{ emit_flag }}=1 uv run {{ worker_id }} signals scan  # -> emitted 0 (no horizon yet)
uv run pytest -q && uv run ruff check .              # green out of the box
```

## Make it real

1. **`src/{{ package_name }}/signals/build.py`** — replace the empty
   `scan_{{ package_name }}_horizon` stub with real forward-looking Signals from
   live domain state, each with a real `due_at`. Add more `@scan_horizon`
   functions and list them in `compose_horizon(...)`. Then flip the
   `xfail` test in `tests/test_signals_build.py` to assert your real signals.
2. **`src/{{ package_name }}/cli/cockpit.py`** — replace the example capability,
   the pulse stub, the Doctor probes, and `capture_state()` with real
   {{ worker_id }} surfaces.
3. **`src/{{ package_name }}/cli/home_hooks.py`** — optionally add worker-owned
   home rows, regions, and key handling. Keep domain policy here; do not add
   worker-specific rules to the shared template.
4. **`src/{{ package_name }}/google_auth.py`** — if the worker needs Google APIs,
   uncomment the matching `CredentialSpec`, keep secret values in the worker's
   config layer, and resolve credentials at the integration boundary.
5. **Go live** — register `{{ worker_id }}` in the bridge roster
   (`Auto-Orchestrator/src/xops/bridge/workers.py`), set `{{ emit_flag }}=1`, and
   add a daily `signals scan` scheduler entry (see clonway-cockpit's
   `docs/onboarding-a-worker.md` §5–6 for the per-shape recipe).

## Acceptance evidence

Before any PR that adds a bespoke screen, shelf, or write walk is reviewed, paste the
five evidence items from
[`docs/generated-worker-acceptance.md`](https://github.com/hearth-care/clonway-cockpit/blob/main/docs/generated-worker-acceptance.md)
in the PR body:

1. **Home frame renders** — first JSON line showing `kind: home` + `schema_version`.
2. **Capability walk** — `kinds` list covering at least one screen beyond home.
3. **No `unstructured`** — `pytest -q tests/test_cockpit_contract.py` output (pass).
4. **Dry-run decline** — `walk.gate{declined,dry_run}` frame from a write-path drive.
5. **Guarded apply / mock** — apply test output; mock assertion proving no live system.

Also: extend `tests/test_cockpit_contract.py` in the **same change** that adds any
shelf or screen — the scaffold's `["q"]` drive is a placeholder to outgrow.
See the acceptance doc's "Growing the gate" section for the per-screen rule.

## Safe-command matrix

Every worker MUST publish `docs/safe-command-matrix.md` in its own repo — one
row per CLI subcommand/flag combination, all eight columns populated. Start from
the worked example in clonway-cockpit's
[`docs/safe-command-matrix.md`](https://github.com/hearth-care/clonway-cockpit/blob/main/docs/safe-command-matrix.md)
(which already covers `{{ worker_id }}` bare, `--agent-stdio`, `--allow-apply`,
and `signals scan`) and extend it with each new command you add. Any PR that adds, renames, or removes a subcommand must
update the matrix in the same change.

